      "message": "Actually, `plat_free` is just a wrapper for `sys_free`.\nTherefore, its parameter should not be defined as `plat_free(void **)`.\nOn the other hand, `PLAT_FREE()` is designed to check for and prevent double-free errors, which is why it is declared with `void **`.\nIts prototype originally evolved from the macro code below:\n```c\n#define PLAT_FREE(x) \\\ndo {\\\n  assert((x) !\u003d NULL);\\\n  plat_free((x));\\\n  (x) \u003d NULL;\\\n} while(0)\n```\nHowever, since `PLAT_FREE` has now been converted into an actual function, its usage has strictly become `PLAT_FREE(void **)`.\nConsequently, it can no longer be used interchangeably with `plat_free`.",
